## Before Writing Any Code

{% include 'base/partials/read-patterns.md.j2' %}

Then scan the existing codebase for similar patterns. Nuxt 4 keeps app code in `app/`
(if the project still has these folders at the root, use those instead):

```
Grep for existing pages:         app/pages/
Grep for existing composables:   app/composables/
Grep for existing components:    app/components/
Grep for existing server routes: server/api/
Grep for shared schemas/types:   shared/
```

Match the existing code style exactly.

## Project Tooling (check once, before the first gate run)

The quality gates need tooling that a fresh Nuxt starter does not ship. If missing, add it:

- **Typecheck** (`npx nuxi typecheck`): needs `vue-tsc` and `typescript` →
  `npm install -D vue-tsc typescript`
- **Lint** (`npm run lint`): needs `@nuxt/eslint` and a `lint` script →
  `npx nuxi module add eslint`, then make sure `eslint.config.mjs` exports `withNuxt()`
  and `package.json` has `"lint": "eslint ."` (`npm pkg set scripts.lint="eslint ."`)
- **Tests** (`npx vitest run`): needs `vitest`, `@nuxt/test-utils`, `@vue/test-utils`,
  `happy-dom` and a `vitest.config.ts` using `defineVitestConfig` (see the tester agent)
{% if variables.state_library == 'Pinia' %}
- **Pinia**: `@pinia/nuxt` in `modules` → `npx nuxi module add pinia` if missing
{% endif %}

## Code Patterns

### Page Pattern

`useFetch` is SSR-safe and must be called at setup time. It returns `status`
(`'idle' | 'pending' | 'success' | 'error'`).

```vue
<!-- app/pages/projects/index.vue -->
<script setup lang="ts">
useHead({ title: 'Projects' });

const { data: projects, status, error } = await useFetch('/api/projects');
</script>

<template>
  <div>
    <h1>Projects</h1>
    <div v-if="status === 'pending'">Loading...</div>
    <div v-else-if="error">Error: {{ "{{ error.message }}" }}</div>
    <ul v-else>
      <li v-for="project in projects" :key="project.id">
        <NuxtLink :to="`/projects/${project.id}`">
          {{ "{{ project.name }}" }}
        </NuxtLink>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</template>
```

### Composable Pattern

`useFetch` / `useAsyncData` belong in setup (directly or via a composable called from
setup). Functions that run later (click handlers, after `onMounted`) use `$fetch`.

```typescript
// app/composables/useProjects.ts
export function useProjects() {
  // SSR-safe read, runs during setup
  const { data: projects, status, error, refresh } = useFetch('/api/projects', {
    key: 'projects',
    default: () => [] as Project[],
  });

  // Imperative calls use $fetch, never useFetch
  async function createProject(input: { name: string; description?: string }) {
    const project = await $fetch('/api/projects', { method: 'POST', body: input });
    await refresh();
    return project;
  }

  return { projects, status, error, refresh, createProject };
}
```

### Server Route Pattern

Validate every input with a Zod schema via `readValidatedBody` / `getValidatedQuery` /
`getValidatedRouterParams`, and authenticate/authorize in the handler.

```typescript
// server/api/projects/index.get.ts
import { projectQuery } from '#shared/schemas/project';

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const user = await requireUser(event);
  const { skip, limit } = await getValidatedQuery(event, projectQuery.parse);

  return db.project.findMany({ where: { ownerId: user.id }, skip, take: limit });
});

// server/api/projects/index.post.ts
import { projectInput } from '#shared/schemas/project';

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const user = await requireUser(event);
  const body = await readValidatedBody(event, projectInput.parse);

  const project = await db.project.create({ data: { ...body, ownerId: user.id } });
  setResponseStatus(event, 201);
  return project;
});

// server/api/projects/[id].get.ts
import { projectParams } from '#shared/schemas/project';

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const user = await requireUser(event);
  const { id } = await getValidatedRouterParams(event, projectParams.parse);
  const project = await db.project.findFirst({ where: { id, ownerId: user.id } });
  if (!project) {
    throw createError({ statusCode: 404, statusMessage: 'Project not found' });
  }
  return project;
});
```

{% if variables.state_library == 'Pinia' %}
### Pinia Store Pattern

Shared client state goes in a setup store in `app/stores/` (full rules in
`pinia.md`). Server data a single page reads stays in `useFetch`.

```typescript
// app/stores/cart.ts
export const useCartStore = defineStore('cart', () => {
  const items = ref<CartItem[]>([]);
  const total = computed(() => items.value.reduce((sum, i) => sum + i.price * i.qty, 0));

  async function load() {
    items.value = await $fetch('/api/cart');
  }

  return { items, total, load };
});
```

Fill it during SSR with `await callOnce('cart', () => cart.load())` and destructure
state with `storeToRefs(cart)`.
{% else %}
### Shared State Pattern

No store library: shared state is `useState` inside a composable (SSR-safe, one
copy per request). Never a module-level `ref`.

```typescript
// app/composables/useCart.ts
export function useCart() {
  const items = useState<CartItem[]>('cart-items', () => []);
  const total = computed(() => items.value.reduce((sum, i) => sum + i.price * i.qty, 0));

  async function load() {
    items.value = await $fetch('/api/cart');
  }

  return { items, total, load };
}
```
{% endif %}

### Layout Pattern

```vue
<!-- app/layouts/default.vue -->
<template>
  <div class="layout">
    <header>
      <nav>
        <NuxtLink to="/">Home</NuxtLink>
        <NuxtLink to="/projects">Projects</NuxtLink>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <main>
      <slot />
    </main>
    <footer>
      <p>&copy; {{ "{{ new Date().getFullYear() }}" }}</p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</template>
```

## Style Rules (MANDATORY)

1. **`<script setup lang="ts">`** - Always use Composition API with `<script setup>`
2. **Auto-imports** - Use Nuxt auto-imports (no manual import of `ref`, `computed`, etc.)
3. **`useFetch` at setup, `$fetch` in handlers** - Never call `useFetch` inside a function that runs later
4. **`status`, not `pending`** - Read `status` from `useFetch` / `useAsyncData`
5. **Server routes** - `server/api/`, file-based routing, input via `readValidatedBody` / `getValidatedQuery` / `getValidatedRouterParams`
6. **Auth in server routes** - Authenticate and authorize in every handler for private data
7. **Composables** - Reusable logic in `app/composables/`
8. **Shared state** - {% if variables.state_library == 'Pinia' %}Pinia setup stores (`defineStore('id', () => {...})`), `storeToRefs` to destructure{% else %}`useState` in composables; no store library{% endif %}; never module-level `ref`s
9. **Named exports** - For composables and utilities
10. **TypeScript strict** - No `any` types
11. **`useHead` / `useSeoMeta`** - For page titles and meta
12. **Auth in two places** - Page middleware for UX, server-route checks for data (`nuxt-auth.md`)
13. **Browser APIs only on the client** - `onMounted`, `import.meta.client`, `<ClientOnly>` (`nuxt-pitfalls.md`)

